  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Myanmar (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar, Malaria, Save the Children Federation, Inc. (STC HQ)This program has the following goals: To reduce malaria morbidity and mortality by 85% and 75% respectively by 2020 relative to 2015 baseline figures. In States/Regions where malaria transmission has been interrupted, the goal is to maintain malaria-free status and prevent re-establishment of local transmission.. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: To reduce reported incidence of malaria to less than 1 case per 1,000 population in all States/Regions by 2020..  Objective 2: To interrupt transmission of falciparum malaria in at least 5 States/Regions by 2020 ( Target States/Regions: Bago, Magway, Yangon, Mon, Mandalay)..  Objective 3: To prevent the emergence of multi-ACT resistant P. falciparum in Myanmar..  Objective 4: To prevent the re-establishment of malaria in areas where transmission has been interrupted.</narrative>
  </description>
